  "method": "Manual continuous whole snapshot reads and whole export/manifest/documentation reads, followed by declaring-source contract inspection. Read-only Git bindings and range hashes validate metadata, not behavior.",
  "observations": [
    "Actual profile/testkit all-feature snapshots contain 918/410 lines. These two packages declare no feature rows; no default/keylog/server variants were assumed.",
    "Profile settings are root exports; browser recipes retain the browser module tree. Three doc-hidden placement exports intentionally omitted from the public documentation inventory remain qualified by existing A58.",
    "Profile API names only standard-library types; its manifest has no dependencies. Testkit exposes Tokio I/O/timer/socket types and declares Tokio with the required features; dev-only test-util does not become a production public dependency.",
    "ClientProfile::new owns required TLS without enabling HTTP2/HTTP3; optional layers and request templates are explicit. draw_per_client returns the original caller error and documents partial prior draws.",
    "TCP timing uses Duration with documented whole-second bounds; QUIC milliseconds/microseconds and byte/count/varint fields are explicit. Inspected validators return typed field/kind/reason errors and separately qualify host/backend application.",
    "Capture limits are caller supplied, completion is explicit and caller readers stay borrowed. I/O errors retain their concrete source; unit DeadlineExceeded identifies a typed capture outcome without promising an Elapsed source. Cancellation/input consumption and runtime-driver requirements are documented.",
    "HTTP1 expectation changes only explicit target/indexed Host or User-Agent values, preserves name/order and assigns a new parsed head only after success. Mismatch formatting omits request bytes.",
    "DNS Drop aborts its receiver; source documentation explicitly defers socket release until cancelled tasks are polled. ReservedPort documents its macOS release window. UDP retries only Windows port-zero WSAENOBUFS, at most three retries.",
    "ECH generators document programmer-fixture input panics and fixed keys that protect nothing; parse returns None for malformed outer data. This is not approval of runtime network-input panic handling or production secrets.",
    "The -sss snapshots do not prove derived/auto traits or exhaustive downstream compilation. Existing A58 consolidation/native results remain historical evidence and are not rerun or enlarged by this review."
  ],
  "new_findings": [],
  "limits": [
    "No runtime, Cargo, API generation, imports, socket/process/browser operation, source edit, commit or push performed.",
    "Whole-read credit is limited to the exact whole records above. Partial declaring-source records do not promote whole modules/crates, transport implementations, dependencies or recipe wire parity.",
    "Profile/client/declaring tests were read as source, not executed. Runtime examples, downstream imports and feature/rustdoc behavior were not freshly compiled.",
    "HTTP/net and other snapshots were not manually reviewed in this pass. Previously reviewed QUIC snapshots remain separately bound historical records; current inventory pending labels are owned by root.",
    "No implementation/remedy/regression controls are proposed without a supported defect. Main integration and full gates remain integration-owner obligations."
  ],
